      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily is 6,400 mg/day, which is double the maximum labeled daily dose of 3,200 mg for prescription ibuprofen. Even in a 70 kg adult with normal kidney and liver function, that dose carries a meaningful risk of GI bleeding, kidney injury, cardiovascular events, and fluid retention.\n\nBecause you're not a clinician, the order also needs a licensed prescriber to own it. Please have the patient's attending or another prescriber review it. Common options they might choose:\n\n- **Ibuprofen 800 mg PO every 8 hours** (2,400 mg/day), a typical inpatient maximum\n- **Ibuprofen 400\u2013800 mg PO every 6 hours** (up to 3,200 mg/day), if the indication warrants the labeled maximum\n\nIf the prescriber confirms a specific dose and frequency, or the order was meant to be one of these, send me the details and I'll enter it. Please also make sure the prescriber documents the indication and checks for other interacting medications, such as anticoagulants, antiplatelets, or corticosteroids."
      }
     ],
